-- V1.8.6 — Agenda et rendez-vous d’équipe (docs/V186_AGENDA_CLUB.md). Applies after 20261128090000 (V1.8.5).
-- A club keeps a private agenda: its administrators propose real meetings (a ride, a run, a session) once or every week, with a fallback
-- plan in case of a change, an optional capacity, and each member answers. After the meeting, each member may say they were there and
-- CHOOSE to link one of their existing sessions to the group's report. Everything is built from bricks that already hold:
--   * The club and its roles (20261030090000): only a club ADMINISTRATOR organises (create, move, switch to the fallback, cancel, restore,
--     cancel or resume a series, renew the invitation link), with the permission check of the club season (CLUB_ADMIN_REQUIRED). Every
--     read and every answer requires a CURRENT membership: a member who left, or was removed, reads nothing (CLUB_NOT_FOUND).
--   * A series is materialised once: a weekly meeting of N occurrences writes N rows at creation (unique (event, n)), each at the same
--     Paris wall-clock time (the change of hour in March and October keeps 18:30 at 18:30). Cancelling a series cancels its future
--     occurrences in place and resuming it restores those same rows: nothing is ever duplicated.
--   * A clear history (private.titan_club_event_changes): creation, every move (from → to), every switch to or from the fallback, every
--     cancellation and restoration, the cancellation and the resumption of a series, with the time. The author is never shown to members.
--   * Answers: « Je viens » (yes), « Peut-être » (maybe), « Je ne viens pas » (no), until the occurrence starts. With a capacity, a « yes »
--     beyond the last place is kept as WAITLIST (in order of answer); a place freed by a change of mind, a departure from the club or an
--     erased account goes to the first one waiting (promoted_at, shown in the social digest). Every answer goes through the club row lock
--     and then the occurrence row lock: two answers for the last place are serialised and the count never exceeds the capacity.
--   * A move or a switch to the fallback keeps the answers and marks them « to confirm » (changed_at > confirmed_at): the member keeps the
--     new time, the fallback and the history, and changes their mind if they wish.
--   * What members read: title, time, duration, general area, fallback, capacity, the COUNTS of answers, their own answer, the history.
--     The precise place (optional, set by the organiser) is read only by administrators and by members who answered yes, maybe or wait,
--     and only until the occurrence ends; never through an expired invitation, never after a departure. Only administrators read who
--     answered what (the public username, as for the club roster they already moderate).
--   * Reminders are optional, per answer (« Me le rappeler »): the social digest shows the meeting in its last 24 hours, nothing is pushed.
--   * The invitation link (code of 8 characters, /social.html?rdv=CODE) opens the meeting for a CURRENT member of the club only while the
--     series has an occurrence to come; otherwise « expired » (a member) or « unavailable » (anyone else, an unknown or renewed code), with no
--     title, no time, no place. Rate-limited, never an error for a wrong code.
--   * The finished card: from the start to 7 days after the end, each current member may declare they were there (or not) and, if they were,
--     link ONE of their own confirmed sessions of that Paris day (private.titan_confirmed_sessions) — or unlink it. Nothing is ever written
--     in the journal (public.training_logs is only read): no session is created, changed or attributed for anyone. The group's report gives
--     the number of answers, of declared presences and of linked sessions; the minutes, the distance and the number of disciplines only from
--     3 linked sessions (the club threshold). Never a name or a session of another member for a member.
--   * No XP, credit, title, ranking or reward. Server flag screens.club_agenda (absent = closed) for create, a yes, a maybe, a reminder, a
--     move, a restoration, a resumption, the invitation link and the digest; « no », presence, linking, cancelling always work. Exported
--     (« clubAgenda ») and erased with the account; an event keeps its history without its organiser (created_by on delete set null).
--     Measure for the pilot: private.titan_club_agenda_measure (counts only: meetings held, confirmed answers, return the next week).
-- Additive. The caller owns the transaction: never BEGIN/COMMIT here.
-- Rollback: drop trigger titan_club_members_agenda on private.titan_club_members, trigger titan_club_event_answers_freed on
